requests.testScript:
pw.test("Status is 200", () => { pw.expect(pw.response.status).toBe(200); });
pw.test("has kpis", () => { pw.expect(typeof pw.response.body.data.kpis).toBe('object'); });
pw.test("has charts", () => { const d = pw.response.body.data; pw.expect(Array.isArray(d.acreageEnrolled)).toBe(true); pw.expect(Array.isArray(d.programSplit)).toBe(true); pw.expect(Array.isArray(d.assessmentTrends)).toBe(true); pw.expect(Array.isArray(d.rhiByProgram)).toBe(true); });

requests.description:
Platform-wide admin analytics in ONE response - headline KPIs (enrolled acreage, farms/farmers/fields enrolled, assessments submitted, completion %, avg RHI, total programs), cumulative acreage over the last 8 months (area chart), enrollment-by-program split (donut, with colors + %), monthly assessment submission/score trends (line), and average RHI per program (bar). All REAL data from the live DB. Needs an ADMIN or SUPER_ADMIN token.

NOTE: the schema has no per-farm "region" column, so RHI is benchmarked per PROGRAM. The `rhiByProgram` items keep the key `region` (the program name) so the existing bar chart works unchanged.

### Expected response (OK 200)

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Admin dashboard fetched.",
  "data": {
    "kpis": {
      "enrolledAcreage": 980,
      "farmsEnrolled": 7,
      "farmersEnrolled": 5,
      "fieldsEnrolled": 7,
      "assessmentsSubmitted": 3,
      "completionPct": 42.9,
      "avgRhi": 60.6,
      "totalPrograms": 1
    },
    "acreageEnrolled": [
      { "month": "Jul", "acres": 980 }
    ],
    "programSplit": [
      { "name": "Govt Rice Scheme", "acres": 920, "value": 100, "color": "#136F3F" }
    ],
    "assessmentTrends": [
      { "month": "Jul", "completion": 3, "score": 60.6 }
    ],
    "rhiByProgram": [
      { "region": "Govt Rice Scheme", "rhi": 61 }
    ]
  }
}
```

